{"author":{"id":"5c16d2edb1bf8ad02dd2ab17aaeb49c2ac57736f65c32cfb0a29a64006e14a7e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791229331,"nonce":"Z16wnOmpRDtflcPA3zKFB9XFsDo=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"IC_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABZbsW1w","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"1160898769d8b93b1a73436f360c85612c9d3baea440e696ba6c20268fe63f76","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/21#issuecomment-6001727191"},"message":"## Navigation Bar\n\nThe app's sections depend on each other in a fixed order: Results depend on Hardware and Energy, which in turn depend on Scope. Navigation should therefore be handled by a wizard with Previous/Next buttons, guiding users to enter information in the correct order. The wizard should remain flexible, however, and allow users to return to any previous step at any time.\n\n1\\. Scope of the assessment\n2a. Hardware inventory\n2b. Energy consumption\n3\\. Results\n\n### About page\nThe welcome page should not be included in the wizard process b ut should be considered a secondary page or even be only a pop up. It should also be renamed to \"About\" instead of \"welcome\".\n### Result page different status\nIn the wizard bar, the Results tab should look different from the other tabs, to signal that completing all the other steps leads to the Results page.\n\n### Option 1 (which I recommend): Unlocking the result button\n\u003cimg width=\"1440\" height=\"120\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68511a77-c589-4447-931d-3a3760dd6fa4\" /\u003e\n\n### Option 2: Timeline\n\u003cimg width=\"1440\" height=\"170\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bd76b710-2f40-4cd1-aa10-2ccdc1baeb14\" /\u003e\n\n### Option 3: Per page color scheme\n\u003cimg width=\"1440\" height=\"140\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f37a9092-d998-4e16-9cf3-b550b60ba025\" /\u003e\n\n### Option 4: Basic\n\u003cimg width=\"850\" height=\"86\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/915420d8-0552-4ed8-9ef1-d7ac314b22a5\" /\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1791229910,"nonce":"En8HM7paN+kODNTxfGSYx5/+O2g=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"IC_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABZb0UuQ","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"bf18a8a735c01fec7f615ffa74ac8284b0c5f0f362a4959c99f6e98f75bb7f36","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/21#issuecomment-6001857721"},"message":"## Boundaries table (excluded/incldued)\n\nThe included and excluded boundaries interface currently doesn't differentiate both options enough making the filling confusing.\n\n\u003cimg width=\"1757\" height=\"417\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fec56f5a-1701-46d7-b31b-44ee82797bc2\" /\u003e\n\n### Option 1 (which I recommend): Words as separator\n\u003cimg width=\"1052\" height=\"399\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6b06b354-c235-4ed0-bd6f-d5c1eae1b6cc\" /\u003e\n\n\u003e redesign this section using words as separators to clarify the input of boundaries and removing the unclear table heading labels\n\n### Option 2: Live report preview\n\n\u003cimg width=\"1200\" height=\"560\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/56473f08-bb50-48fa-b66b-40f95db117b8\" /\u003e\n\n### Option 3: Per section color scheme\n\u003cimg width=\"1200\" height=\"700\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d83d5ac1-3c97-4ff9-b3ce-efae24d4f672\" /\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1791230352,"nonce":"QTtS+p1iFHbohIWnF6g1YmFS6jc=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"IC_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABZb6WqQ","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"a8fc26ac410962aba4e8e9b56a5fa367ff14bf60d6ffd7cf59e78d009882a579","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/21#issuecomment-6001956521"},"message":"## Color scheme \n\u003cimg width=\"1065\" height=\"594\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b7ea31b5-a5a3-4f36-8ca2-6f128a178aa9\" /\u003e\n\nFor the color scheme i propose 2 colors representing `Embodied` and `Operational` with 5 shades each for all inner categories. \n\n**For Embodied:**\n- Server\n- Compute Server\n- Storage\n- Network Switch\n- Spare Parts\n\n**For operational:**\nThe datasets formatted {abbreviation}-{dataset} \n\nI Suggest this red and blue but other colors could be chosen as long as the shading/tagging system is respected and colors are in a harmonious tone.\n\n## Colorblind\nInclude a global colorblind mode using echarts decals (like in co2 calculator) to differentiate the color of the colorscale above. \n\n\u003cimg width=\"1344\" height=\"650\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6626462b-d096-44ef-9a1d-ba71488ad1e1\" /\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1791230425,"nonce":"Y8oHTkK8fzmrCq+dr7/tL967l1E=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"IC_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABZb7XFw","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"ffb5892019d287d079a0c6ae736afe495736051d2623603cfe35ed3de5e1b527","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/21#issuecomment-6001973015"},"message":"@juliapaolini  Here are my design propositions according for the 3 points we discussed. Feel free to comment, choose, give suggestion for all them :)","files":null}]}